  "summary": "Dutchess County, NY officials \u2014 the DA, sheriff, and county executive \u2014 announced they will not renew the county's Flock license-plate reader contract after a public forum where speakers uniformly opposed the technology, and will divert $500,000 budgeted for the cameras to other services. The article also reports Newburgh City Council's pending vote to dissolve its Flock contract and discusses related camera programs in Beacon, Peekskill, and Putnam County.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Dutchess County district attorney and sheriff announced on Friday (Sept. 25) that, following a public forum in Pleasant Valley, they no longer support the county's use of Flock license-plate readers.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "If the district attorney and the sheriff no longer believe that Flock Safety technology is a tool that they need, I stand by them in that decision",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "substantial concerns regarding access to and sharing of locally collected ALPR [automated license-plate reader] information across jurisdictions and with other law-enforcement agencies, including federal agencies",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
